  "test": "Read the 7-segment code first (also shown on the thermostat). Thermistors: unplug the harness and ohm per pins, compare with the chart. Transducers: measure VDC plugged in (pin 1-3 = 5 V, pin 2-3 vs chart). Reset: cycle R power.",
  "notes": "Pin pair 4-3 (black sleeve) = outdoor ambient RT13 in every source. The manuals disagree about pins 6-5 and 2-1: the terminal table, the sensor-operation text, the E416 text and Figure (Temperature Sensor Specification) each put the coil/liquid sensor and the 10K resistor(s) in different places. Trace the brown-sleeve wires before condemning anything on 6-5 or 2-1; a fixed resistor reads about 10K ohms at any temperature, a sensor changes with temperature. EL18XPV specifics: Table 6 (p.34) says COIL and DIS are 10K resistors; p.75 and E416 say a 10K resistor on pins 5-6; Figure 49 (p.76) shows the liquid-line sensor on 6-5 and the resistor on 2-1. Inverter LED: -024/-036 red ON green OFF = normal; -048/-060 both ON = normal; both OFF = inverter not powered. Wiring diagram (p.50): R7 resistor on the LIQ position, RT13 on AMB, RT21 on COIL (no pin numbers printed). LPS: p.57 text says no low pressure switch and terminals not jumpered, but the diagram shows S87 on LPS; p.57 also lists 'low pressure trip 25 / reset 40' against E410's 40/90 cut-out/cut-in.",
  "gaps": [
   "6-pin harness pins 6-5 vs 2-1 conflict",
   "Inverter board connectors and inverter error codes (E423+) not mapped",
   "Compressor winding table values not tied to sizes"
  ],
