  "notes": "Pin pair 4-3 (black sleeve) = outdoor ambient RT13 in every source. The manuals disagree about pins 6-5 and 2-1: the terminal table, the sensor-operation text, the E416 text and Figure (Temperature Sensor Specification) each put the coil/liquid sensor and the 10K resistor(s) in different places. Trace the brown-sleeve wires before condemning anything on 6-5 or 2-1; a fixed resistor reads about 10K ohms at any temperature, a sensor changes with temperature. EL19KPV: Table 6 (p.40) says COIL and DIS are 10K resistors; E416 says resistor on 5-6; Figure 46 (p.78) shows coil 6-5 brown and \"discharge N/A\" on 2-1. Replacement outdoor control kit: 508718-01 (EL18KCV/EL19KPV). Wiring diagram (p.55): R7 resistor on the LIQ position, RT13 on AMB, RT21 on COIL (no pin numbers printed). The sensor-operation text (p.77) says R7 is on pins 5-6 and RT21 is also on 5-6; the figure drawing shows the resistor on 5-6 and the liquid-line sensor on 1-2; the figure table says coil 6-5, none 2-1.",
