  "test": "Status: 2-digit major + 1 minor on the 3-digit display; the LED shows the major code (short flashes = first digit, long = second). Last 7 faults: MENU to FLt. Component test (idle, R removed, door switch held): Ct - Pur inducer high 10 s, HSI 15 s, Fn blower 50% 10 s, End inducer low 10 s (p56 Table 23).",
  "notes": "Same HK42FZ board figure (A221519) and same schematic as 59TP6C, re-traced on 59TP7A-03SI p57. Service label (p55) lists 34.1 and 34.5-34.8 (no 34.2/34.3), 52 = SAT, 53 = RAT, 23.4 LPS stuck closed, 23.5 HPS stuck closed; the troubleshooting guide prints RAT as 52.1/52.2 (p74) and HPS stuck as 23.2 (p75) - label numbering used. Troubleshooting also lists 25.7 non-condensing program detected. Legend calls IDM 'ECM' while both diagrams draw a two-speed inducer with run capacitor (diagram kept). Also matches 927TA (same board/diagram: new-manuals/carrier-3/bryant-927ta-03si.pdf vs carrier-59tp7a-03si.pdf: board figure p.28, service label p.55, wiring diagram p.57 identical apart from header).",
