  "test": "If the A2L sensor is not connected the system will not operate. On a leak the sensor switches both internal relays: outdoor compressor off, indoor blower on at cooling speed, alarm output on; blower stays on 5 minutes after the leak clears (may cycle with a small leak). Sensor is powered from the transformer secondary; all 24 VAC for external devices (R) comes from sensor pin 6. Diagram shows the relays in the ALARM state. Sensor LEDs (10498530 Table 2): green steady = warm-up; green heartbeat = normal; amber steady = power-up fail; green+red blinking = near end of life; red blinking = end of life (replace) or internal diagnostic fail (power cycle resets an internal fault); red steady = DTLV alarm (leak); green+amber heartbeat = out of operating range. End of life is permanent - a power cycle will not recover it. Replace only with the Nordyne-specified sensor; check the area with a suitable refrigerant detector first.",
